1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,025
This is a photograph of a mountain range.

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:06,366
A hiker took it on a cold, clear morning.

3
00:00:06,386 --> 00:00:08,098
Nothing unusual about it.

4
00:00:08,818 --> 00:00:10,077
Except... right here.

5
00:00:11,247 --> 00:00:12,024
Four pixels.

6
00:00:12,044 --> 00:00:14,152
A tiny, pale shape on the ridge.

7
00:00:14,922 --> 00:00:17,819
Years after this photo was taken, those four

8
00:00:17,839 --> 00:00:20,339
pixels got the man who took it killed.

9
00:00:22,409 --> 00:00:26,576
This is the complete story of SCP-096.

10
00:00:30,546 --> 00:00:33,366
The Foundation files it as Euclid.

11
00:00:33,386 --> 00:00:34,118
Humanoid.

12
00:00:34,138 --> 00:00:37,125
2.38 meters tall, nearly eight feet.

13
00:00:37,745 --> 00:00:38,485
It's thin.

14
00:00:38,505 --> 00:00:40,081
Malnourished, almost.

15
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:42,664
Its arms are about 1.5 meters long

16
00:00:42,684 --> 00:00:45,096
each, far too long for its body.

17
00:00:45,716 --> 00:00:47,951
Its skin has almost no pigment.

18
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:48,533
No hair.

19
00:00:48,553 --> 00:00:51,007
Its eyes have no color at all, and

20
00:00:51,027 --> 00:00:53,336
nobody knows if it can even see.

21
00:00:53,956 --> 00:00:54,883
And its jaw...

22
00:00:54,903 --> 00:00:56,981
can open to four times the size

23
00:00:57,001 --> 00:00:58,334
of a normal human's.

24
00:00:59,104 --> 00:01:00,644
Researchers found no sign of

25
00:01:00,664 --> 00:01:01,869
higher brain function.

26
00:01:02,589 --> 00:01:03,971
But none of that is what

27
00:01:03,991 --> 00:01:05,081
makes it dangerous.

28
00:01:05,951 --> 00:01:08,037
Most days, it's completely calm.

29
00:01:08,057 --> 00:01:10,735
It paces by the eastern wall of its cell.

30
00:01:11,205 --> 00:01:12,197
Back and forth.

31
00:01:12,217 --> 00:01:13,210
Back and forth.

32
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:15,831
And that's the scariest part.

33
00:01:15,851 --> 00:01:17,380
Because it stays calm...

34
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,832
right up until somebody sees its face.

35
00:01:23,302 --> 00:01:24,256
Here's the rule.

36
00:01:24,776 --> 00:01:28,651
If you see 096's face, in person, on video,

37
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:32,636
or even in a photograph, you become what the

38
00:01:32,656 --> 00:01:35,082
Foundation calls SCP-096-1.

39
00:01:35,852 --> 00:01:37,792
The moment that happens, it changes.

40
00:01:38,312 --> 00:01:40,665
It covers its face with its hands.

41
00:01:40,685 --> 00:01:42,131
It screams. It cries.

42
00:01:42,151 --> 00:01:44,923
It babbles things nobody can understand.

43
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:47,296
About one to two minutes later...

44
00:01:47,966 --> 00:01:49,053
it starts running.

45
00:01:50,223 --> 00:01:52,356
It doesn't need to know where you are.

46
00:01:52,376 --> 00:01:53,149
It just knows.

47
00:01:53,169 --> 00:01:54,905
Any direction, any distance, it

48
00:01:54,925 --> 00:01:56,209
heads straight for you.

49
00:01:56,729 --> 00:02:00,007
Recorded speeds start at 35 km/h.

50
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:02,405
The top speed? Redacted.

51
00:02:03,175 --> 00:02:05,397
No material, no method, nothing the

52
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:07,959
Foundation has tried has ever stopped it

53
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:09,561
from reaching its target.

54
00:02:10,281 --> 00:02:11,919
And it doesn't matter how

55
00:02:11,939 --> 00:02:13,179
small the image is.

56
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:15,102
Or how long ago it was taken.

57
00:02:15,972 --> 00:02:18,290
And when it does, the file says only this.

58
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:22,642
In 100% of cases, no traces were left.

59
00:02:23,812 --> 00:02:25,035
Then it sits down.

60
00:02:25,055 --> 00:02:25,932
Calms itself.

61
00:02:25,952 --> 00:02:27,933
And quietly tries to go home.

62
00:02:28,803 --> 00:02:30,850
One small mercy: drawings of its

63
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:32,271
face don't trigger it.

64
00:02:32,291 --> 00:02:33,563
Only the real thing.

65
00:02:34,083 --> 00:02:36,322
Which is why you can watch this video.

66
00:02:37,042 --> 00:02:37,890
Probably.

67
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,613
So how do you contain something like that?

68
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:46,919
SCP-096 lives in a sealed steel

69
00:02:46,939 --> 00:02:49,450
cube, 5 meters on every side.

70
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:50,236
Airtight.

71
00:02:50,756 --> 00:02:52,277
Every week, staff check every

72
00:02:52,297 --> 00:02:53,446
inch of it for cracks.

73
00:02:54,166 --> 00:02:56,461
And one rule is never broken.

74
00:02:56,481 --> 00:02:58,137
No cameras. No video.

75
00:02:58,157 --> 00:03:00,532
No optical devices of any kind

76
00:03:00,552 --> 00:03:02,368
inside that cell. Ever.

77
00:03:03,138 --> 00:03:05,459
Guards rely on pressure sensors and

78
00:03:05,479 --> 00:03:07,064
laser detectors instead.

79
00:03:07,084 --> 00:03:08,802
They know it's in there...

80
00:03:08,822 --> 00:03:10,608
without ever looking at it.

81
00:03:11,278 --> 00:03:13,621
Even a photo of it needs approval

82
00:03:13,641 --> 00:03:15,339
from the very top of the

83
00:03:15,359 --> 00:03:17,272
Foundation, the O5 Council.

84
00:03:17,942 --> 00:03:19,852
But it wasn't always in a box.

85
00:03:19,872 --> 00:03:21,782
Someone had to catch it first.

86
00:03:25,152 --> 00:03:28,003
This next part comes from a recorded

87
00:03:28,023 --> 00:03:31,512
interview with a retired captain, the leader

88
00:03:31,532 --> 00:03:34,143
of the team sent to bring 096 in.

89
00:03:34,163 --> 00:03:35,259
Team Zulu 9-A.

90
00:03:35,979 --> 00:03:37,206
Two helicopters.

91
00:03:37,226 --> 00:03:39,931
A frozen wasteland, far below zero.

92
00:03:40,451 --> 00:03:42,624
They spot the target north of their

93
00:03:42,644 --> 00:03:44,816
patrol path, facing away from them.

94
00:03:45,436 --> 00:03:47,354
And the first thing the captain

95
00:03:47,374 --> 00:03:49,041
notices is that it's naked.

96
00:03:49,061 --> 00:03:49,854
In that cold.

97
00:03:49,874 --> 00:03:51,291
And it isn't shivering.

98
00:03:52,161 --> 00:03:53,717
They move in to bag it.

99
00:03:53,737 --> 00:03:56,526
Right then, the captain's radio goes off.

100
00:03:56,546 --> 00:03:57,760
A doctor, calling.

101
00:03:57,780 --> 00:03:59,404
He turns away to answer.

102
00:04:00,074 --> 00:04:01,590
That call saved his life.

103
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:04,342
Because his squad didn't turn away.

104
00:04:04,362 --> 00:04:05,449
They saw its face.

105
00:04:07,219 --> 00:04:08,573
It tore through the squad.

106
00:04:09,093 --> 00:04:10,870
They hit it with rifles.

107
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,367
An anti-tank rocket.

108
00:04:12,387 --> 00:04:15,062
A helicopter machine gun, around 600

109
00:04:15,082 --> 00:04:17,832
.50-caliber rounds in twenty seconds,

110
00:04:17,852 --> 00:04:19,554
by the captain's count.

111
00:04:20,424 --> 00:04:21,505
None of it mattered.

112
00:04:22,775 --> 00:04:25,679
It only stopped when the second team, Zulu

113
00:04:25,699 --> 00:04:28,117
9-B, did something nobody expected.

114
00:04:28,637 --> 00:04:30,403
They slipped a bag over its head.

115
00:04:31,273 --> 00:04:32,710
And it... just sat down.

116
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:33,438
Quiet. Calm.

117
00:04:33,458 --> 00:04:35,016
Like nothing had happened.

118
00:04:36,086 --> 00:04:37,898
At the end of the interview, the

119
00:04:37,918 --> 00:04:39,959
doctor offers to show the captain an

120
00:04:39,979 --> 00:04:41,562
artist's sketch of its face.

121
00:04:42,082 --> 00:04:43,014
He refuses.

122
00:04:43,034 --> 00:04:45,609
Then he formally requests that

123
00:04:45,629 --> 00:04:47,167
096 be terminated.

124
00:04:50,637 --> 00:04:52,337
Remember that mountain photo?

125
00:04:52,357 --> 00:04:53,998
This is where it comes back.

126
00:04:54,718 --> 00:04:56,274
Incident 096-1-A.

127
00:04:56,294 --> 00:04:59,518
SCP-096 breaks out of its cell at a

128
00:04:59,538 --> 00:05:01,836
Foundation research site.

129
00:05:02,356 --> 00:05:04,797
The staff who see its face don't make it.

130
00:05:04,817 --> 00:05:06,597
The site is sealed and gassed.

131
00:05:07,417 --> 00:05:09,552
Then it's out, running across the desert.

132
00:05:10,022 --> 00:05:12,603
Helicopters chase it, and fall behind.

133
00:05:12,623 --> 00:05:13,629
Snipers hit it.

134
00:05:13,649 --> 00:05:15,066
It doesn't slow down.

135
00:05:15,736 --> 00:05:18,617
Task force teams race ahead in tiltrotor

136
00:05:18,637 --> 00:05:21,445
aircraft, evacuating towns in its path.

137
00:05:21,915 --> 00:05:24,056
It crosses Interstate 40, smashing

138
00:05:24,076 --> 00:05:25,645
straight through traffic.

139
00:05:26,415 --> 00:05:27,085
Its target?

140
00:05:27,105 --> 00:05:28,401
A former mountaineer.

141
00:05:28,971 --> 00:05:31,386
Years earlier, he'd photographed

142
00:05:31,406 --> 00:05:32,984
a mountain landscape.

143
00:05:33,004 --> 00:05:35,494
And somewhere on that ridge, four

144
00:05:35,514 --> 00:05:37,625
pixels wide, was 096's face.

145
00:05:38,295 --> 00:05:40,343
He'd been given special goggles

146
00:05:40,363 --> 00:05:42,412
designed to scramble the image.

147
00:05:42,432 --> 00:05:43,213
They failed.

148
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:44,814
Just for a split second.

149
00:05:45,434 --> 00:05:46,428
That was enough.

150
00:05:47,598 --> 00:05:49,478
SCP-096 reached him in a

151
00:05:49,498 --> 00:05:51,062
crowded town square.

152
00:05:51,082 --> 00:05:53,992
The task force lost most of its team.

153
00:05:54,862 --> 00:05:57,626
In the end, it was a single door gunner

154
00:05:57,646 --> 00:06:00,482
who landed by the highway, where 096 was

155
00:06:00,502 --> 00:06:02,267
tearing into a minivan...

156
00:06:02,287 --> 00:06:04,481
and pulled a bag over its head.

157
00:06:05,201 --> 00:06:06,876
Just like the first time.

158
00:06:06,896 --> 00:06:07,689
It sat down.

159
00:06:07,709 --> 00:06:08,638
It went quiet.

160
00:06:12,108 --> 00:06:14,326
Even the Foundation doesn't

161
00:06:14,346 --> 00:06:16,067
fully understand 096.

162
00:06:16,737 --> 00:06:18,609
Its eyes have no pigment.

163
00:06:18,629 --> 00:06:19,517
Is it blind?

164
00:06:19,537 --> 00:06:20,500
Nobody knows.

165
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,619
It finds its victims anyway.

166
00:06:23,289 --> 00:06:25,463
It shows no higher brain function.

167
00:06:25,483 --> 00:06:28,109
And yet, when it's triggered, it babbles,

168
00:06:28,129 --> 00:06:30,239
almost like it's trying to speak.

169
00:06:30,909 --> 00:06:32,905
Why does a photograph trigger it,

170
00:06:32,925 --> 00:06:34,248
but a drawing doesn't?

171
00:06:34,268 --> 00:06:35,470
The file never says.

172
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,564
And after every attack, it tries to

173
00:06:38,584 --> 00:06:40,659
return to its natural habitat.

174
00:06:40,679 --> 00:06:42,335
Where is that? Redacted.

175
00:06:43,105 --> 00:06:44,737
Some think it's suffering.

176
00:06:44,757 --> 00:06:46,262
That the crying is real.

177
00:06:46,282 --> 00:06:47,533
That all it wants...

178
00:06:47,553 --> 00:06:48,804
is to never be seen.

179
00:06:52,274 --> 00:06:53,833
So why not just destroy it?

180
00:06:54,453 --> 00:06:57,035
A termination order was approved, and the

181
00:06:57,055 --> 00:06:58,940
doctor sent to carry it out...

182
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,590
is heavily implied to have

183
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:01,606
never come back.

184
00:07:02,426 --> 00:07:04,041
600 rounds. Rockets.

185
00:07:04,061 --> 00:07:04,695
Snipers.

186
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:06,249
Nothing has worked.

187
00:07:06,869 --> 00:07:09,713
Today, 096 sits in its steel cube,

188
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:11,988
pacing by the eastern wall.

189
00:07:12,008 --> 00:07:12,662
Waiting.

190
00:07:13,382 --> 00:07:14,830
For someone. Somewhere.

191
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:15,851
To see its face.

192
00:07:17,821 --> 00:07:20,495
That's the complete story of SCP-096.

193
00:07:20,515 --> 00:07:22,388
Would you have survived...

194
00:07:22,408 --> 00:07:24,208
or would you have looked?

195
00:07:24,228 --> 00:07:25,956
Tell me in the comments.

196
00:07:26,576 --> 00:07:28,616
If you made it this far, you're

197
00:07:28,636 --> 00:07:30,344
braver than team Zulu 9-A.

198
00:07:31,014 --> 00:07:32,592
Next time: SCP-173.

199
00:07:32,612 --> 00:07:36,125
The statue that only moves when you blink.

200
00:07:36,145 --> 00:07:38,733
Subscribe so you don't miss it.
